// Chapter 7: DAX measures for the Bramblewood model in Power BI
// Tables: Sales (fact), Products, Stores, and a 'Date' table marked as a date table,
// related to Sales[order_date]. Sales has a calculated column:
//   Line Revenue = Sales[units] * Sales[unit_price] * (1 - Sales[discount])

Total Revenue = SUM ( Sales[Line Revenue] )

Total Cost =
SUMX ( Sales, Sales[units] * RELATED ( Products[unit_cost] ) )

Gross Margin % =
DIVIDE ( [Total Revenue] - [Total Cost], [Total Revenue] )

Revenue LY =
CALCULATE ( [Total Revenue], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR ( 'Date'[Date] ) )

Revenue YoY % = DIVIDE ( [Total Revenue] - [Revenue LY], [Revenue LY] )

Orders = DISTINCTCOUNT ( Sales[order_id] )

Average Order Value = DIVIDE ( [Total Revenue], [Orders] )
